terminal-ended` when the list no longer holds the terminal and `terminal-failed` when it does (a start whose session is not listed afterwards is `terminal-not-started`), so no text of tmux or of a validator reaches the page, which says the catalog sentence of the word (`state/shared/answers/terminal-words.ts`); a refused resize is said on the bar of the tab that owns the terminal. A start sets the session's name, its resume mark and a task's mark in the `new-session` invocation itself, joined by tmux's `;`, so a command that ends at once still leaves a named, marked session. The list the `sessions` payload carries is republished when a terminal's name, title, icon, colour, task mark, exit status or pane process changes (`#took` in `server/machine/pty/channel.ts`), so a task terminal run again that ends with the status it ended with before is a change the pages are told of.
