 - `local.yml` carries `hub` (the research hub's absolute path, default two directories above `tools/oculus`) and `port` (default 8790; 8787 is the cockpit's and is never used). The text catalog reaches the browser as the page's data at first load and afterwards by push over the socket like every other YAML (the portfolio watcher covers `config/` as well as the hub); the browser never fetches the YAML as a file.
 - One tree per page, every split child foldable to its edge through one control and expandable again, the folded state saved with the layout. There is no panel beside the tree: what a side panel would hold (shift-click in the Views catalogue, a session detail opened from a card, a project's editor and deposit opened from its card) opens in a new pane to the right of the active one, and the next one joins that pane as a tab while it is still open, so opening the editor from five cards is one pane of five tabs rather than five panes. A saved layout of two trees is read as one: a page keeps its main area as the root when the panel holds nothing, and otherwise is a split of the two at the shares the panel had, with the panel child folded when the panel was hidden.
 - A page shows other pages. A leaf of a page's tree is another page, drawn where it sits with a header naming it and the one control that stops showing it there; it is the same page and never a copy, so a tab opened in it is open wherever that page shows and switching to it shows the same arrangement. A page never contains itself, directly or through another page, and is drawn at most once on a screen; a drop or a menu item that would break either rule is not offered, and a page taken out, or closed from the Pages view, gives its space back to the neighbour it was split from. Two page leaves side by side show two pages next to each other. A nested page is reached by focus and not by a digit: a bare digit is the rail page of its place. Every store operation that names a path names the page it addresses, the page on screen when it names none, so a pane carries the page it belongs to beside its path and a view opened while reading inside a shown page lands in that page. The pane menu is the keyboard path to showing a page and a page's row dragged from the Pages view onto a pane's edge is the pointer path.
-- Pages: the workbench is one of several pages, each a whole arrangement with a name, and the saved layout is the list of pages plus which one is current plus the floats, so the layout tree of "Layout as data" is unchanged and gains a level above it. The rail's buttons are the pages of `rail:`, each tied to its arrangement by key; a browser with no saved layout draws no page until the configuration names the first, and starts on it; the Pages view makes, renames and closes pages, one explorer row per page (`ui/tree/TreeItem.svelte` in a `TreeView`), whose press shows the page; a row dragged past the drag threshold and released over itself shows nothing, by the rule the Views catalogue keeps for its cards (`views/system/workbench/row-press.ts`). The Views catalogue on the System page opens a view on the page shown before that page, which the layout store tracks and does not save; a catalogue moved onto another page opens on that page. An entry is also opened on the catalogue's own page: dragged onto a pane there (a `view` drag of `state/workbench/drag.svelte.ts`), or through its right-click menu's Open on this page and Open beside on this page. None of them covers the catalogue. A view asked for in the catalogue's own pane opens in another pane of the page, or beside the catalogue when its pane is the page's only one, and a view already open in another pane of the page is activated where it is (`openAway` and `openNextTo` of `state/workbench/layout/open/away.ts`). Switching pages unmounts the hidden page's views, which rebuild from the stores when it returns (a terminal repaints its scrollback), so nothing is drawn twice and no hidden terminal holds a client. The digits 1 to 9 show the rail page of their place, Ctrl with a digit switches the tab in the focused pane, and a group's `chord` letter before a digit opens the entry of that place in the group (`f`, `m`, `p`, `e`, `s`, `c`, `l`, `r`, `t`, `h` and `y`, one per rail page); `direct_chord` counts the entries of a group with no `chord`, and every shipped group has one. A rail button's menu, and a rail page's row of the Pages view, reset that page to its arrangement, and Settings resets every rail page, removes the pages of buttons the rail no longer has and puts the floats of `config/layout.yml` back in place of the floats held (`resetPlan`, `resetAsk` and `resetAfterAsking` of `state/workbench/navigation/pages.ts`, `resetPage` and `resetPages` of the layout store); each asks first through a confirmation naming the pages, then asks each tab of those pages holding unsaved text the question closing that tab asks, one at a time, and a no to any ends the reset with nothing changed; a page the reader made is never touched.
